{"name":"Sunset Boulevard","hex":"#ff9607","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sunset","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The moment each evening when the sun disappears below the western horizon.","The changes in color of the sky before and after sunset."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To phase out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunset"},{"term":"boulevard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A broad, well-paved and landscaped thoroughfare.","The landscaping on the sides of a boulevard or other thoroughfare."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boulevard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunset Boulevard","blocks":[{"text":"Sunset Boulevard is a boulevard in the central and western part of Los Angeles, California, United States. Stretching from the Pacific Coast Highway in Pacific Palisades to Figueroa Street in downtown Los Angeles, it is a major thoroughfare in the cities of Beverly Hills and West Hollywood, as well as several districts in Los Angeles itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Sunsetblvdnearvine.jpg/330px-Sunsetblvdnearvine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset_Boulevard"},{"title":"Sunset Boulevard (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sunset Boulevard is a 1950 American black comedy film noir directed by Billy Wilder and co-written by Wilder, Charles Brackett, and D. M. Marshman Jr. It is named after a major street that runs through Hollywood and western Los Angeles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Sunset_Boulevard_%281950_poster%29.jpg/330px-Sunset_Boulevard_%281950_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset_Boulevard_(film)"},{"title":"Sunset","blocks":[{"text":"Sunset is the disappearance of the Sun at the end of the Sun path, below the horizon of the Earth due to its rotation. As viewed from everywhere on Earth, it is a phenomenon that happens approximately once every 24 hours, except in areas close to the poles. The equinox Sun sets due west at the moment of both the spring and autumn equinoxes. As viewed from the Northern Hemisphere, the Sun sets to the northwest in the spring and summer, and to the southwest in the autumn and winter; these seasons are reversed for the Southern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg/330px-Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset"},{"title":"Boulevard","blocks":[{"text":"A boulevard is a type of broad avenue planted with rows of trees, or in parts of North America, any urban highway or wide road in a commercial district."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Park_Avenue_01.jpg/330px-Park_Avenue_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boulevard"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Sunsetblvd.jpg/500px-Sunsetblvd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Sunsetblvd.jpg/500px-Sunsetblvd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Signs along the Sunset Strip","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunsetblvd.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Sunset_Tower%2C_8358_Sunset_Blvd._West_Hollywood_2383.jpg/500px-Sunset_Tower%2C_8358_Sunset_Blvd._West_Hollywood_2383.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Sunset_Tower%2C_8358_Suns